.TH "ET\-USER\-BACKUP" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-user\-backup \- back up EmComm Tools user data
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R] creates a compressed archive of selected user
data from the current user\(cqs home directory.
.PP
The backup includes EmComm Tools configuration, Winlink email,
Reticulum, MeshChat, Partyline, and NomadNet data, when present.
Directories that do not exist are skipped.
.PP
The archive is written to the user\(cqs home directory and includes the
hostname and current date in its filename.
If a backup for the same hostname and date already exists, the operator
is prompted before it is overwritten.
Declining the prompt cancels the backup.
.PP
After creating the archive, \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R] checks that its
contents can be listed.
It then displays the directories included in the backup and offers to
show the complete file list.
.SH BACKUP CONTENTS
The following directories are included when they exist:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.config/emcomm\-tools\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.config/partyline\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.local/share/emcomm\-tools\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.local/share/pat\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.nomadnetwork\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum\-meshchat\f[R]
.PP
Files outside these directories are not backed up.
Back them up separately if needed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-user\-backup
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R] before reinstalling EmComm Tools, moving
to another computer, or making changes to user configuration.
.SH BACKUP RECOMMENDATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Run \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R] periodically to preserve Winlink email,
Reticulum identities, messages, and other supported user data.
.IP \(bu 2
Copy the compressed archive to an external USB drive or another computer
for safekeeping.
.IP \(bu 2
EmComm Tools does not support direct upgrades between releases.
Use \f[B]et\-user\-backup\f[R] and \f[B]et\-user\-restore\f[R] to
migrate most core user data when installing a new release.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/etc\-user\-backup\-HOSTNAME\-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz\f[R]
The compressed backup archive, named using the system hostname and the
date on which the backup was created.
